:: Missing Children Intro
The <<personsimple>> who answers the door looks to you with a concerned and tired look. "The missing children? Listen, I really don't have time for this. I have my own children and I can't deal with you distracting me."
<br><br>
You look past the <<person>>'s frame into <<his>> small house. You hear something... strange inside, like the sound of dragging chains. The <<personsimple>>, seeming to hear the sound as well, turns around in a hurry and rushes back into <<his>> home. 
<br><br>
The house falls silent, nothing to break up the sound of a grieving <<father>> and the breeze through an open window.
<br><br>
<<link [[Examine outside the window (0:10)|Missing Children]]>><<endevent>><<pass 10>><</link>>

:: Missing Children
You walk around the small Domus home and look around the window. Some claw markings remain on the frame and large heavy hoof prints are embedded into the hard winter soil.
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggery gte 800 or $transformationParts.traits.sharpEyes is "default" or $transformationParts.dragon.eyes isnot "disabled">>
As you look closer, a barely visible trail is evident where chains have been dragged through the dirt. Black fur clings to a nearby branch. Whatever this is, it's definitely not human.
<br><br>
<</if>>
You follow the tracks from house to house. You can hear the muffled wails through the walls. It's heartbreaking to hear, so you try to tone it out.
<br><br>
Eventually the tracks disappear into the forest. It seems whatever has been kidnapping the children has retreated to possibly its home. Trailing it may be a bad idea without sufficient preparation.
<br><br>
<<link [[Follow the trail into the forest (2:00)|Missing Children 2]]>><<pass 120>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Give up the request|Missing Children Fail]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Missing Children 2
<<if !$per_npc.krampus>>
	<<beastNEWinit 1 creature>>
    <<set $monster to 1>>
	<<set $NPCList[0].monster to "monster">>
    <<set $NPCList[0].fullDescription to "Krampus">>
    <<set $NPCList[0].name to "Krampus">>
