:: Crying Baby Intro
"Oh thank god." <<He>> says, pushing a hand through greying hair. "Come in, please."
<br><br>
The <<personsimple>> steps aside and guides you inside to a couch. The manor is fairly large and fancy yet the owner looks worse than even people living in the flats.
<br><br>
After a moment, the <<person>> continues, "As I wrote in my post, for several days now, I have been hearing the sound of a crying baby from near the forest. I haven't got a wink of sleep in four days now and I am losing it. Please could you make the noises stop?"
<br><br>
Tears well in the <<personsimple>>'s eyes as <<he>> begs, a position you doubt <<he>> has ever assumed in <<his>> life.
<br><br>
<<link [[Investigate the back, near the forest|Crying Baby]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Crying Baby
You follow the hallway out to the lavish backyard, which fades into wooded land as the forest encroaches onto the property. You can hear the soft muffled cries of something that sounds like a newborn.
<br><br>
The cries grow louder as you cautiously step into the forest. You follow a small path as you draw closer to the loud cries. You come to an unmarked grave you can tell was dug recently, the earth still loose from digging.
<br><br>
As you draw close you feel a tearing pain at your back as something sinks claws into you. <<gpain>><<pain 5>>
<br><br>
A sound of a small voice whispers wet into your ear, "Bring my body to the churchyard... I need to be buried..."
<br><br>
The weight on your back slowly grows as the claws sink further into your back. <<gpain>><<pain 5>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Dig up the unmarked grave|Crying Baby 2]]>><</link>>

:: Crying Baby 2
You begin to dig into the shallow grave and find a tiny skeleton buried not too deep. It seems to be the abandoned body of an infant. <<gtrauma>><<trauma 5>>
<br><br>
You pick up the bones, it seems the myling wants you to bring these to the churchyard within the forest.
<br><br>
<<link [[Begin the journey to the churchyard|Crying Baby Forest]]>><<set $forest to 0>><</link>>

